    "narrative": "The clear focal point for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who anchors the lineup with an elite score of 85.94. Facing a favorable matchup against Zach Agnos (xERA 5.15), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-leverage #2 spot in the order and a robust xwOBA of .376, making him our primary engine for both stolen bases and run production. Joining him in the \"strong\" tier are **James Wood** (62.77) and **Mickey Moniak** (60.60). **James Wood** continues to provide high-upside value leading off, and despite a neutral platoon, his ability to manufacture runs outweighs the risk of facing a solid arm in David Peterson. While **Mickey Moniak** faces a potential platoon disadvantage against Eduardo Rodriguez, his spot in the #2 hole and positive park factors keep his efficiency firmly above the 60 threshold.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Kyle Karros** (55.22), who sat right on the edge of our starting threshold. While his platoon advantage against Rodriguez is helpful, the combination of a low #8 spot in the order and the overall strength of our outfield depth pushed him to the bench in favor of optimizing our categorical needs. We are exercising caution with **Austin Riley** (53.89) today; despite being a high-pedigree bat, his poor BvP history against Sandy Alcantara (34 PA) and an assumed #7 order slot keep his ceiling capped. We are keeping a close eye on the official lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Austin Riley**, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces slight volatility to their scoring projections. With **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Brice Turang** unavailable due to injury or off-days, we are leaning heavily on our current starters to capitalize on favorable matchups against high-xERA pitchers like Agnos to maintain our 5x5 pace.",
